glsl: a default precision for sampler2DShadow under GL_EXT_shadow_samplers in GLSL ES 1.00

GL_EXT_shadow_samplers adds the sampler type sampler2DShadow to GLSL ES 1.00,
whose section 4.5.3 allows a default precision for int, float and any sampler
type. Mesa lexes the keyword whenever it is used, but adds the type to the symbol
table only for GLSL 1.10 and GLSL ES 3.00, so the default precision statement,
which looks the type up by name, fails with "default precision statements
apply only to float, int, and opaque types" even with the extension enabled.
Add the type when the extension is enabled.

ioquake3's OpenGL 2 renderer with r_PreferOpenglES 1 hits it on every driver
that exposes the extension (llvmpipe too).

--- a/src/compiler/glsl/builtin_types.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/glsl/builtin_types.cpp
@@ -311,6 +311,13 @@
       add_type(symbols, &glsl_type_builtin_sampler2DRectShadow);
    }
 
+   /* GL_EXT_shadow_samplers brings sampler2DShadow to GLSL ES 1.00.  The
+    * lexer takes the keyword anyway, but a default precision statement looks
+    * the type up by name ("precision lowp sampler2DShadow;", which the
+    * extension's own example uses). */
+   if (state->EXT_shadow_samplers_enable)
+      add_type(symbols, &glsl_type_builtin_sampler2DShadow);
+
    if (state->EXT_gpu_shader4_enable) {
       add_type(symbols, &glsl_type_builtin_uint);
       add_type(symbols, &glsl_type_builtin_uvec2);
